// Deviates from the sheet's own `Explosion` variant, same reasoning
// acid_splash.ron in this folder already documents:
// `CharacterAbility::Explosion` (common/src/states/explosion.rs) always
// detonates centered on the CASTER's own position -- it has no
// target-point field, only a `radius`. This spell's 18 m range (a burst
// thrown at a chosen point, not self-centered) contradicts that, so it
// uses `GroundAoe` instead, the real "detonate at a chosen point within
// range" primitive (see dark_star.ron, the sibling shape this was cloned
// from).
//
// `GroundAoe` also hardcodes `DamageKind::Energy`
// (common/src/states/ground_aoe.rs) -- no RON-configurable `damage_kind`
// field exists on this variant -- so despite the Thunder flavor text this
// deals generic Energy damage under the hood, same drift acid_splash.ron
// documents.
//
// Circle 2: damage/energy set below fireball.ron's circle-3 numbers in
// this same folder (48 dmg / 90 energy), matching the one-circle-lower
// relationship real D&D's own Shatter (2nd) has to Fireball (3rd).
// Flagged for wave-close-out balance review.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 45.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.45,
    delay: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    max_range: 18.0,
    radius: 3.0,
    min_falloff: 0.3,
    damage: 30,
    poise: 15,
    knockback: (strength: 8, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: Roll,
    rooted_cast: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
